  150: 'Miyazawa Kenji said his stories were all **gathered in woods and fields and along railway lines, given to him by rainbows and moonlight**. Did you bring home a story today?',
  151: 'Miyazawa Kenji opened “Spring and Asura” with **the phenomenon called “I” is one blue illumination of a hypothetical organic alternating-current lamp**. Today, too, one small light flickering on.',
  152: 'In “Wild Pear,” Miyazawa Kenji has two little crabs whisper underwater, **Kuramubon laughed. Kuramubon laughed kapu-kapu**. Some words feel good even when you don’t know what they mean.',
