  158: 'Yosano Akiko sang, **in the shape of little golden birds, the ginkgo leaves fall on the hill in the evening sun**. The season when ginkgo leaves land like birds.',
  159: 'Yosano Akiko sang of **a field of autumn flowers under the evening moon, where I went out feeling, somehow, that someone was waiting for me**. Some evenings just call you outside.',
